<%# A school's years.

    **Each row is provisioned data, not a preference.** Creating a school year writes four quarters and
    removing it destroys them. The edit form used to carry a `collection_check_boxes` on `year_ids`, which did
    both silently - and raised `PG::ForeignKeyViolation`, a 500, when the year had a classroom, because the
    join was deleted before `restrict_with_error` could speak. Both measured.

    A list row, not a card each: a name with some metadata and one action is Polaris's ResourceList, and a
    card per row on a page that already has surfaces is the card soup this document forbids.

    Locals:
      school       - the school
      school_years - loaded, with :year, :classrooms and :quarters
      addable      - years not yet added, newest first
      manage       - render the add and remove controls. **False on the show page**, because a show page
                     shows: the same controls in two places is two things to keep in step, and the write
                     belongs where the rest of the writing happens.

    The controls cannot live *inside* the school's form even on the edit page: `button_to` renders a whole
    `<form>` and the add is a form of its own, and the browser drops a nested one - the button would silently
    submit the outer form. So this sits below the form as a sibling section, which is what this document says
    to do rather than nesting. %>
<section aria-labelledby="school-years-heading">
  <h2 id="school-years-heading" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">School years</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
    <% if manage %>
      Changes here apply immediately. Adding a year sets up its four quarters; removing one deletes them, so
      a year with classrooms in it cannot be removed.
    <% else %>
      Each year has its own quarters. Add or remove them on the edit page.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <div class="tw-card mt-3 divide-y divide-slate-100" data-testid="school-years">
    <% school_years.each do |school_year| %>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 p-4">
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">
            <%= school_year.year_name %>
            <% if school_year.year.current? %>
              <%= render "components/ui/badge", label: "Current", tone: :info %>
            <% end %>
          </p>
          <%# Quarters only. The classroom count appears on the right, where it is the reason removal is
              refused - stating it in both places had the blocked row reading "1 classroom" twice. %>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600"><%= pluralize(school_year.quarters.size, "quarter") %></p>
        </div>

        <% if manage %>
          <%# The consequence is in the confirmation because it is not recoverable and not obvious: four
              quarters go with the year. A row that cannot act says why in its place rather than offering a
              control that would only refuse - the column-of-dashes rule. %>
          <% if school_year.removable? %>
            <%= button_to "Remove",
                          admin_school_school_year_path(school, school_year),
                          method: :delete,
                          class: ghost_class(:danger),
                          data: { testid: "remove-school-year",
                                  turbo_confirm: "Remove #{school_year.year_name} from #{school.name}?" \
                                                 "\n\nIts " \
                                                 "#{pluralize(school_year.quarters.size, 'quarter')} " \
                                                 "will be deleted. This cannot be undone." } %>
          <% else %>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
              In use by <%= pluralize(school_year.classrooms.size, "classroom") %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
        <% elsif !school_year.removable? %>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600">
            In use by <%= pluralize(school_year.classrooms.size, "classroom") %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% if school_years.empty? %>
      <div class="p-4">
        <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                   locals: { icon: "calendar-check",
                             title: "No school years yet",
                             body: manage ? "Add one to set up its quarters." : "Add one on the edit page." } do %><% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <%# The add control, as the card's last row - the shape a table footer uses. Every year not already
        added, newest first: a select can carry the whole list, so no year is unreachable and there is no
        window to invent. %>
    <% if manage && addable.any? %>
      <%= form_with url: admin_school_school_years_path(school), method: :post,
                    class: "flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3 p-4" do |f| %>
        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
          <%= f.label :year_id, "Add a school year", class: "tw-label-primary" %>
          <%= f.select :year_id,
                       options_for_select(addable.map { |y| [year_option_text(y), y.id] }),
                       {}, class: "tw-input-primary mt-1" %>
        </div>
        <%= f.submit "Add school year", class: "tw-btn-secondary" %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
